    Bug 1983328 - Fix failing EWS mark-as-junk test. r=edicharry

    The inconsistency in the test failures was due to not `await`ing
    `TestUtils.waitForCondition`. Once I fixed this I noted a couple of issues
    causing the test to keep failing:

    * we didn't resync the messages for the source folder, meaning the target
      messages wouldn't disappear from that folder (until the next sync)
    * our custom ordering logic for message list changes meant changes weren't
      replayed locally in the right order

    Regarding the latter, I decided to remove that custom ordering logic and just
    use the ordering provided by the server, which I'd expect to be chronological.

    I've also taken the liberty to extend this test a bit to make sure our
    implementation replicates the behaviour of `MarkAsJunk` on more recent server
    versions (i.e. marking as junk moves from the original folder to the junk
    folder, but marking as not junk moves from the junk folder to the inbox folder).

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D264232

